---
title: Fava beans and pork
category: Mains
cuisine: Portuguese
servings: 4
tags:
  - meat
  - Portugal
  - marinade
difficulty: average
prep time: 30 minutes
cook time: 1 hour
created: 2026-05-29
updated: 2026-05-29
---

Cut @pork shoulder{500%g} into chunks.

Place the meat into a bowl, and season with @garlic{2%cloves}(minced), @paprika{1%tsp}, @bay leaf{1}, @salt{}, @black pepper{}(freshly ground), and @white wine{1%dl}. Mix together, cover, and leave to marinate in the refrigerator overnight.

Place @fava beans{750%g} into a heatproof bowl and cover with boiling water.

In the meantime, drain the pork meat while keeping the marinade for later.

Place a #pot{} over medium heat and melt @lard{30%g} in it.

Add the marinated pork and cook until browned on all sides.

Add @onion{1}(finely chopped) to the pot, and cook on low until soft.

Add @tomato purée{200%ml} and the marinade, cover, and keep cooking on low, stirring occasionally until the meat is tender and cooked through.

> Add water if it starts to become too dry.

Drain the beans and remove the shells. Add them to the meat, and cook for ~{10%minutes}, stirring the pot occasionally. Salt to taste.

Finally, add @tomato{300%g}(roughly chopped and deseeded).

Sprinkle with @coriander leaves{}(chopped) before serving.